  "source_dataset": "MIMIC_IV_NOTE",
  "text": "Allergies:\nBactrim\n\nChief Complaint:\nAbdominal pain, nausea and vomiting\n\nHistory of Present Illness:\n___ w/ hx DM1 has insulin pump, presumed gastroparesis, frequent \nUTIs, recent upper GI in ___ w/ atrophic mucosa and 1 month PPI \ntrial which she completed at the end of ___, p/w 1 wk N/V decr \nPO tolerance, and epigastric pain intermittent->constant x 3 \ndays. recent central chest burning a/w emesis, not worse with \nexercise. Has not eaten in 3 days, limited liquids and none \ntoday. +diarrhea x 1 day which resolved three days prior to \npresentation. Upon presentation to the ED:  VS 97.6 83 134/82 16 \n100%. She received dilaudid 1 mg x 1, 0.5 x1, \nmylanta, APAP, donnatal, viscous lidocaine, protonix, macrobid, \nzofran and IVF x 3 L. Her BS also dipped to 52 but improved with \nIV dextrose.  Despite this she was unable to tolerate po intake \nand was admitted. Prior to the development of sx one week ago \nshe was doing well with dietary modifications, eating small \nmeals and not eating too late. \nShe thinks that the trigger may have been eating an entire \nveggie burger very late since she had to wait two hours for food \nto be served when she was away organizing a ___ conference. \nShe current denies sx of a UTI such as urinary frequency, \ndysuria which is what she commonly has when she has a UTI. \n.\nREVIEW OF SYSTEMS:\nCONSTITUTIONAL:  As per HPI and no fevers or chills. She doesn't \nthink that she has lost any weight.\nHEENT:  [X] All normal\nRESPIRATORY:  [X] All normal\nCARDIAC:  [X] All normal\nGI:  As per HPI. She also denies constipation\nGU:  [X] All normal\nSKIN:  [X] All normal\nMUSCULOSKELETAL:  [X] All normal\nNEURO:  [X] All normal\nENDOCRINE:  [X] All normal\nHEME/LYMPH:  [X]  All normal\nPSYCH:  [X] All normal\nAll other systems negative except as noted above\n\nBrief Hospital Course:\nThe patient is a ___ year old female with h/o type I DM on \ninsulin pump c/b gastroparesis largely well controlled by diet \nwith occasional zofran use, recent diagnosis of gastritis s/p 1 \nmonth of acid suppresion therapy who presents with abdominal \npain, n/v/ x 1 week in the setting of eating a veggie burger \nlate at night c/w flare of gastroparesis/GERD.  Her symptoms \nwere treated symptomatically and with PPI, with significant \nimprovement.  She was able to tolerate a full diet prior to \ndischarge with no further n/v.  She was continued on her insulin \npump and course was complicated by hypoglycemia which resolved \nwith PO intake.  She was found to have a + UA however was \nasymptomatic therefore she was not started on antibiotics for \nUTI.  \n\n>30 min spent on dc related activities\n\nDischarge Diagnosis:\nGastroparesis flare\nGERD\nT1 Diabetes",
